  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Silenced No More Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Silenced No More &#x2013; Confronting Violence against Women and Young Girls&#x201d; tackles taboos head-on and speaks inconvenient truths, by giving a voice to victims who have experienced SGBV and FGM. The theatre performances and campaign will foster critical thinking among the Kenyan public to re-examine harmful practices and actions against women, and generate new perspective and dialogues that will expose to the Kenyan audiences&#x2019; stories seldom told, and be part of normalizing conversations around these difficult topics. Through engagements with the local theatre and art scene, the project also aims to inspire Kenyan cultural practitioners to tackle and take up difficult themes in art and theatre. In addition to tackling these important issues, the long-term vision is also to build a vibrant Danish-Kenya performing Arts network creatively operating between the two countries.</narrative>
  </description>
